<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niagara-on-the-Lake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niagara-on-the-Lake is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niagara-river">Niagara River</a> enters Lake Ontario. Settled by Loyalists after the American Revolution and named Newark, it was the first capital of Upper Canada from 1792 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-graves-simcoe">John Graves Simcoe</a> moved the capital to York, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toronto">Toronto</a>, in 1796. American troops burned it in December 1813 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-1812">War of 1812</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/niagara-on-the-lake.jpg" alt="Niagara-on-the-Lake" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paste Let’s have a chat. / Paste at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Niagara_on_the_lake.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
